<title>CANADA: Laidlaw pays about US$130 mln for Vancom.</title>
<headline>Laidlaw pays about US$130 mln for Vancom.</headline>
<dateline>BURLINGTON, Ontario 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transportation company Laidlaw Inc paid about US$130 million, plus or minus 10 percent, to acquire privately held U.S. school bus firm Vancom Inc, Laidlaw Transit chief operating officer John Grainger said on Monday.</p>
<p>The added revenues would start to show up on Laidlaw's bottom line in fiscal 1998, Grainger told Reuters in a phone interview. Laidlaw announced the acquisition earlier today.</p>
<p>Laidlaw class B shares slipped 0.10 to 17.90 on almost 600,000 shares on the Toronto Stock Exchange in afternoon trading today.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
